0.08 0.08 0.08 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 55 643 Td (Network Cables and Crimping can be understood by following a communication from its source) Tj ET
0.08 0.08 0.08 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 55 628 Td (through the relevant interfaces and protocol layers. Each device processes only the) Tj ET
0.08 0.08 0.08 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 55 613 Td (information needed for its role. Correct operation depends on consistent addressing,) Tj ET
0.08 0.08 0.08 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 55 598 Td (compatible link settings, correct service configuration, and a return path for replies.) Tj ET
0.08 0.08 0.08 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 55 577 Td (At the link layer, frames carry local delivery information such as source and destination) Tj ET
0.08 0.08 0.08 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 55 562 Td (MAC addresses. At the network layer, IP addresses and routing decisions identify the path) Tj ET
0.08 0.08 0.08 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 55 547 Td (between subnets. Transport and application protocols provide the end-to-end service when) Tj ET
0.08 0.08 0.08 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 55 532 Td (required. A failure at any layer can prevent the expected application behavior.) Tj ET
